// Regression: a program's `#[symbol]` definition must be emitted under the exact
// ABI name and must be the body that runs.
//
// Two traps, both of which the earlier bugs fell into:
//
//  1. `pickle_str_len` is declared here, so THIS body must run. Rust's
//     `pickle_str_len` is correct and returns the real length, so a linker that
//     silently kept the archive copy would print a plausible number and this
//     test would still "pass". The override returns a fixed sentinel instead,
//     which no correct archive implementation can produce. Rule recorded in
//     MEMORIES: make the two implementations distinguishable, then observe
//     which one runs.
//
//  2. `pickle_str_from_bytes` and `pickle_str_cmp` are NOT declared here, so the
//     archive copies must still win. If the override leaked to undeclared names,
//     this program would concatenate with a body that has no business running.
//
// SCOPE, verified by mutation on 2026-10-04 — read this before trusting the test
// to cover more than it does. Negating the `#[symbol]` check in
// `compiler/emit.pkl::itemSymbol` makes this print "FAIL: override did not win",
// so it genuinely pins the emit path. Disabling the override list
// (`cli/buildlib.pkl::overrideSymbols`) does NOT make it fail, because the
// program object is merged at index 0 and so wins every collision by ordering
// alone. `progOverrides` (compiler a38b3cb) therefore governs *relocation
// redirection* for archive-internal call sites, not definition selection; this
// fixture does not cover that. Covering it needs an archive-internal call to a
// name the program also defines — a case that needs a purpose-built archive, not
// a program-only fixture.
//
// `len(s) != 31337` proves (1). Building a runtime string and comparing it prove
// (2), since `+` lowers to pickle_str_from_bytes and `!=` to pickle_str_cmp.

module symoverride_main

// Must win over the archive: this value cannot come from Rust's real impl.
#[symbol("pickle_str_len")]
fn lyingStrLen(s: *int) -> int {
    return 31337
}

fn main() {
    let s = "abc"
    let n = len(s)
    if (n != 31337) {
        println("FAIL: override did not win")
        return
    }
    // Exercise the undeclared paths: the archive must still supply these.
    // `+` lowers to pickle_str_from_bytes and `!=` to pickle_str_cmp, so this
    // one comparison covers both archive bodies that were NOT overridden.
    let joined = "ab" + "cd"
    if (joined != "abcd") {
        println("FAIL: an undeclared archive body was displaced")
        return
    }
    println("SYM_OVERRIDE_OK")
}